course: dictionary
lesson: 11887
title: Brevity: saying more with less
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Brevity is a formal word for using few words. When you speak or write with brevity, you say what you mean clearly and leave out extra words. It is a noun, and it is uncountable, so you say "brevity", not "brevities".
explain: «She answered the question with brevity: "Yes, I will."» That is two words and a full answer, with nothing wasted. Brevity is about how many words you use. A brief answer can still be polite and kind.
explain: Brevity can also describe time. «We noticed the brevity of the summer, which was over in a few weeks.» Here it means how short something lasts, like «the brevity of life». To check a new word, swap in a simpler one, such as "shortness", and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Brevity means using few words, and being short and to the point.
fact: Brevity can also mean how short a time something lasts, as in «the brevity of life».
fact: «Brevity is the soul of wit» is a famous line from Shakespeare's play Hamlet. It means that saying something clearly and briefly shows clever thinking.
fact: In exams and formal writing, «for brevity» means «to keep it short».
exercise: «The reply was a model of brevity: "Sorry, I am late."» What does brevity mean here? | *Using few words and getting straight to the point | Speaking very loudly | Telling a long story with lots of detail | Using lots of long, fancy words
exercise: Ella writes a very long letter. Her teacher says, "Write with more brevity." What should Ella do? | Add a drawing on every line | Add more long words to sound clever | *Cut the extra words and keep only what matters | Write the whole letter in capital letters
exercise: «The brevity of the summer made it feel like one week.» What does brevity mean here? | How much rain fell in the summer | *How short a time the summer lasted | How many people came to the summer fair | How hot the summer was
test: Which answer shows brevity best? | *"Yes." | "Well, yes, I suppose so, if you really want me to" | "Yes, yes, I think that might possibly be right" | "I agree, and I think you are right too"
test: In an exam, what does «for brevity» mean? | To write in capital letters | *To keep it short | To make the answer longer | To add a picture
exam: What does «the brevity of life» mean? | How long life lasts forever | How happy life feels | *How short life is | How many people live on Earth
